shakespeare/data/ — the "tiny Shakespeare" corpus
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

About 1.1 MB of dialogue from the plays of William Shakespeare, as one
stream of text. The plays themselves are long out of copyright.

The particular file — this selection, in this order, with speaker names
inline — is the one distributed with Andrej Karpathy's char-rnn:

    https://github.com/karpathy/char-rnn
    data/tinyshakespeare/input.txt

obtained on 2026-09-12, redistributed unmodified. char-rnn is MIT
licensed. SHA-256 of the uncompressed text:

    86c4e6aa9db7c042ec79f339dcb96d42b0075e16b8fc2e86bf0ca57e2dc565ed

It has been the standard toy corpus for character-level language models
since 2015, which is the reason to use it here: a reader can compare
what our model produces against a decade of published samples from the
same text.

